  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Direct object clitic pronouns (lo, la, los, las, me, te, nos) are unstressed pronouns that attach closely to verbs and replace a direct object noun. \nIn affirmative commands and infinitives, they follow the verb (e.g., *Lléveme al hotel*); otherwise, they precede the conjugated verb (*No la tengo*). \nThey agree in gender and number with the noun they replace."
    }
